00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:54.020
On a similar note though, I guess just to play devil's advocate here.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:13:15.000
Um, when also, also when it comes to puzzle games, like you can, like, even though the particular arrangement of any puzzle may be different, um, if it's using the same tool set, like, like a game like this, where it's mostly about moving blocks.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:22.320
Shooting enemies, uh, to, to sort of neutralize them and avoiding, uh, obstacles.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:32.360
Uh, if you're just using those same tools to, to make your puzzle, it can also like just the whole concept can get a little bland.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:45.060
I don't think it did, but in a, in a way that, uh, like say portal portal two is so different because, you know, making just different, like test changes.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:49.760
Uh, you're really just sort of rearranging chairs.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:55.200
Uh, and it's not really making anything that is really challenging you.

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:58.520
Like the original did when the concept was still new.

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:08.940
Um, I do think that there was room in this game for new concepts and it's been so long that maybe I missed some that were new concepts.

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:16.180
So maybe this is unjust criticism, but I also see how that can be used as a complaint.

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:29.360
Yeah. I mean, I, I, I think that like personally, like my personal taste for something like this is I'd like a happy medium, you know, I'd like, you know, yeah, make some changes based up, but I don't, I don't necessarily want a format change.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:34.100
