But just starting from the ground up and saying, yeah, it's Adventures of Lolo, but this time Lolo can jump.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:31.120
You know, it's like, is that worth exploring?

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:34.040
Or is that like, that's not what Adventures of Lolo is.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:41.100
Like, it's about moving, it's about moving blocks and, you know, getting out of tight situations and maneuvering enemies.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:43.280
Well, I think that's totally valid.

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:45.420
Yeah, I think that's worth exploring.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:49.760
If you've, if you design puzzles around that, you've added a new way of thinking.

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:55.060
Like, totally. Like, that is the, that's the add the goo gun for Portal.

00:18:55.480 --> 00:19:00.960
And that was sort of the difference I was making there of a game that switched it up a bit.

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:04.960
That it wasn't like, oh, now Portal is a looter shooter.

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:09.420
Which I think is sort of the complaint Joe would have had.

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:10.640
Like, oh, just leave it the same.

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:12.020
Make it, leave it a puzzle game.

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:14.440
And not Final Fantasy 16.

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:21.820
But, and that's sort of, I would have appreciated that out of Adventures of Lolo 2.

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:25.160
I'm not, I don't hate that that's all that there is.

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:29.060
Because, um, is mostly just Adventures of Lolo 1 stuff.

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:35.360
In the same way that I wouldn't have hated Portal 1, Portal 2 just being, uh, test chambers.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:38.520
Um, but, yes.

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:41.000
I think that that would be totally valid.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:46.740
That'd be a good idea. That'd be an interesting, uh, mechanic to add to something like this.

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:50.460
Yeah, definitely. And, like, I don't, I don't, I'm not sure if any of us know.

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:56.620
But, like, it's been so long since I've played Adventures of Lolo 1 that I also don't remember if, like, anything is new in this.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:20:03.360
So, like, maybe if I had just finished Adventures of Lolo 1 and then started this, I would get burnt out a lot more quickly.

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:06.460
Because I'd be like, okay, I, there's nothing new here.

00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:07.880
