00:25:44.540 --> 00:25:53.200
So, like, I think that that's all, like, and I only got to, like, Tower 6 or something in this, so I don't think I'm, like, not even, like, halfway through this game.

00:25:53.340 --> 00:26:09.840
So, like, maybe they keep doing it, but, like, my want for a game like this is just, like, keep introducing new stuff that, like, that throws me for a loop every time that I have to, like, make me, like, have to relearn how to think about the game just because of what's coming at me in different levels.

00:26:10.760 --> 00:26:14.520
Yeah, I mean, I think, again, that gives you a lot of permutations.

00:26:14.520 --> 00:26:37.000
To have, like, a new enemy to add to the mix, like, yeah, technically there are millions of different ways you can arrange a puzzle room, and I don't particularly think that that means that it's infinitely replayable because eventually those ideas are going to get stale.

00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:39.320
But I think if you're going to add...

00:26:39.840 --> 00:26:47.340
